__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MOVEMENT_LABELS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TOPIC_BANK",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}});var o=r(d[0]);const t=(0,o.localize)({god:"Who God is and what He asks",heart:"What is happening in my heart",gospel:"Where the gospel meets me"}),s=(0,o.localize)([{id:"anger",title:"Anger",heartFocus:"Anger usually rises when something I want badly is blocked, and I start to act as if I'm the judge.",counselorNote:null,passages:["James 4:1\u20133","Ephesians 4:26\u201332","James 1:19\u201320","Romans 12:17\u201321","Psalm 37:1\u20138"],openers:["When was the last time you felt really frustrated? What happened?","What do the people closest to you notice when you get upset?"],movements:{god:["God is \"slow to anger.\" What does it mean to you that God is patient with you?","When God gets angry, it's always about what is truly wrong. How is that different from what usually sets you off?","God says vengeance belongs to Him. How does it feel to leave justice in His hands?","What does God ask of you in how you speak when you're upset?"],heart:["In that moment, what did you want so much that you were willing to sin to get it, or angry when you didn't?","What were you telling yourself about the other person, about yourself, and about God?","Where do you feel you have the right to be in charge, respected, or comfortable?","If you're honest, who were you trusting to make things right: God or yourself?"],gospel:["Jesus was wronged, yet He trusted Himself to the Father, who judges justly. What would it look like to follow Him the next time?","God has forgiven you a great debt. How does that change the way you see what was done to you?","What would a gentle answer sound like in the conversation you're dreading?","Who could you go to this week to ask forgiveness, without explaining yourself?"]},keywords:["angry","anger","furious","mad","yell","rage","frustrat","temper"]},{id:"fear-and-anxiety",title:"Fear and Anxiety",heartFocus:"Anxiety often grows when I try to carry tomorrow on my own and forget that the Father is near and in control.",counselorNote:null,passages:["Matthew 6:25\u201334","Philippians 4:4\u20139","1 Peter 5:6\u20137","Isaiah 41:10","Psalm 56:3\u20134"],openers:["What has been taking up most of your thinking lately?","When do you notice the worry the most: at night, at work, or somewhere else?"],movements:{god:["Jesus says the Father feeds the birds and knows what you need. What do you think the Father is like toward you?","God is present in your future already. How does that change the \"what ifs\"?","God invites you to bring everything to Him in prayer. What keeps you from doing that?","What does God call you to do today, as opposed to tomorrow?"],heart:["What are you afraid of losing? What would it mean to you if you did?","Whose approval, security, or control has become something you feel you must have?","When the worry comes, what do you usually tell yourself about God?","What do you reach for to feel safe, other than the Lord?"],gospel:["If God didn't spare His own Son for you, what does that say about whether He will care for you now?","What would it look like to humble yourself and hand this particular worry to Him today?","What is true, right, and good that you could fill your mind with when the worry starts?","What one act of love toward someone else could you do this week, even while you're afraid?"]},keywords:["anxious","anxiety","worry","worried","afraid","fear","panic","nervous"]},{id:"depression",title:"Depression",heartFocus:"In the dark, it's easy to feel that God is distant and that my life is defined by this weight. God meets sufferers with tenderness and calls them to hope.",counselorNote:"Always ask about physical health and safety too, and refer to a doctor when needed.",passages:["Psalm 42\u201343","Psalm 88","Lamentations 3:19\u201333","2 Corinthians 4:7\u201318","1 Kings 19:1\u201318"],openers:["How have your days been feeling lately, honestly?","What's been the hardest part of the week for you?"],movements:{god:["The psalms let God's people cry out to Him without pretending. What would your honest prayer sound like right now?","God cared for Elijah with sleep and food before He spoke to him. What does that show you about how God treats the weary?","God's mercies are new every morning. Where have you seen even a small one recently?","What does it mean that God is near to the brokenhearted, even when you can't feel it?"],heart:["What are you telling yourself about your life, your future, and God when it's darkest?","Is there a hope or dream that has been lost and that you feel you can't live without?","Is there anything you're carrying alone, like guilt, a hurt, or a secret, that has grown heavier?","Where have you pulled away from God or from people? What do you think that has cost you?"],gospel:["Jesus was \"a man of sorrows.\" How does it help to know He understands this from the inside?","What would it look like to tell your soul to hope in God, even before your feelings follow?","What is one small, faithful step for this week: a walk, a call, a meal with someone, worship on Sunday?","Who could walk with you through this so you are not alone in it?"]},keywords:["depress","hopeless","numb","empty","dark","can't get out of bed","no energy","sad"]},{id:"marriage-conflict",title:"Marriage Conflict",heartFocus:"Fights between spouses usually come from desires inside each of us that have grown too large, more than from the issue we're arguing about.",counselorNote:null,passages:["Ephesians 5:21\u201333","James 4:1\u201310","Colossians 3:12\u201319","1 Peter 3:1\u20139","Matthew 7:1\u20135"],openers:["What first drew you to each other?","When things are going well between you, what does that look like?"],movements:{god:["Marriage is meant to show how Christ loves His church. What does that say about why your marriage matters?","How does Christ love His people when they are hard to love?","What does God ask of you in this marriage, no matter what your spouse does?","God is the one who joined you. How does that change how you see your spouse?"],heart:["In your last big argument, what did you want that you weren't getting?","What do you most expect your spouse to give you that only God can truly give?","Where have you been focused on the speck in your spouse's eye?","What do you tend to do when you feel unloved or disrespected: attack, withdraw, or keep score?"],gospel:["Christ moved toward you while you were still turned away. What would it look like to move toward your spouse first?","What is one thing you need to confess to your spouse without adding \"but\"?","How could you speak to your spouse this week in a way that builds them up?","What does forgiveness look like in your home: not a feeling, but a promise you keep?"]},keywords:["my wife","my husband","spouse","marriage","divorce","argue","fight"]},{id:"pornography",title:"Pornography",heartFocus:"Pornography promises comfort, escape, or power without cost, and it trains the heart to love a counterfeit. Christ offers real freedom and a clean heart.",counselorNote:null,passages:["Matthew 5:27\u201330","1 Thessalonians 4:3\u20138","1 Corinthians 6:12\u201320","Romans 6:11\u201314","Psalm 51"],openers:["What made you willing to talk about this today?","How long has this been part of your life, and who else knows?"],movements:{god:["God made sex good, as a gift within marriage. What has pornography taught you about it instead?","Your body belongs to the Lord. What does that mean for how you use it?","Jesus speaks about the heart, not only actions. Why do you think He does that?","God is holy, and He is also the God who receives sinners. How do you hold those two together?"],heart:["What are you usually feeling right before you go looking: lonely, stressed, bored, angry, rejected?","What does pornography promise you in those moments? Does it keep its promise?","What have you been loving or wanting more than God and more than real people?","Where do you hide or make excuses, and what are you afraid would happen if you were fully known?"],gospel:["After David's sin, he asked God for a clean heart. What would you want to say to God about this?","In Christ, you are dead to sin and alive to God. How does that change what you believe you can do?","Who will you ask to walk with you in honest accountability, as a brother or sister and not a police officer?","What good thing could you pursue in the moments when temptation usually comes?"]},keywords:["porn","pornography","lust","explicit"]},{id:"grief",title:"Grief",heartFocus:"Grief is love that has lost something. God doesn't rush us through it. He grieves with us and gives us a hope that death can't take.",counselorNote:null,passages:["John 11:17\u201344","1 Thessalonians 4:13\u201318","Psalm 34:18","Revelation 21:1\u20135","2 Corinthians 1:3\u20137"],openers:["Would you tell me about the one you lost?","What has each day been like since then?"],movements:{god:["Jesus wept at His friend's grave, even though He knew He would raise him. What does that tell you about Him?","God is called the God of all comfort. Where have you looked for comfort, and where have you found it?","God allows us to grieve, but not like those without hope. What's the difference?","How does God hold both your sorrow and your future?"],heart:["What questions or accusations have you wanted to bring to God?","Is there anything you feel guilty or angry about related to this loss?","Where has grief made it hard to trust God or to want Him?","What have you used to numb the pain?"],gospel:["Christ died and rose again. What does that promise you about death and about the one you lost?","God will wipe away every tear. What would it be like to let that hope sit beside your sorrow?","Who has God given you to grieve with, and how could you let them in?","How might God use your comfort someday to comfort someone else?"]},keywords:["died","death","passed away","funeral","grief","grieving","miss her","miss him","loss"]},{id:"guilt-and-shame",title:"Guilt and Shame",heartFocus:"Guilt says \"I did wrong.\" Shame says \"I am unclean and exposed.\" God answers both: forgiveness for the guilty and covering for the ashamed.",counselorNote:null,passages:["Psalm 32","1 John 1:5\u20132:2","Romans 8:1\u20134","Isaiah 1:18","Hebrews 12:1\u20132"],openers:["Is there something you've been carrying that's hard to talk about?","When you think about your past, what feelings come up?"],movements:{god:["God is light, and there is no darkness in Him. Why might that feel frightening, and why might it be good news?","God is faithful and just to forgive when we confess. What does \"just\" mean there?","In the garden, God covered Adam and Eve's shame. What does that show you about His heart?","What does God ask of you about the things you've hidden?"],heart:["Do you feel more guilty before God, or more ashamed before people? Whose opinion weighs most?","Have you been trying to pay for what you did by punishing yourself or working harder?","Is there any sin you haven't confessed, or any you keep confessing because you don't believe it's forgiven?","Is some of your shame about what was done to you rather than what you did?"],gospel:["Jesus endured the cross and despised the shame. What did He do with your shame?","If there is now no condemnation for those in Christ, what voice have you been listening to instead?","What would it look like to live this week as someone forgiven and clean?","Is there anyone you need to make things right with, out of freedom and not fear?"]},keywords:["guilt","guilty","shame","ashamed","regret","forgive me"]},{id:"bitterness-and-unforgiveness",title:"Bitterness and Unforgiveness",heartFocus:"Bitterness grows when I keep replaying a wrong and hold the debt myself. Forgiveness hands the debt to God, who forgave me far more.",counselorNote:null,passages:["Matthew 18:21\u201335","Ephesians 4:31\u201332","Hebrews 12:14\u201315","Romans 12:17\u201321","Genesis 50:15\u201321"],openers:["Is there someone who hurt you that you find yourself thinking about often?","What happened?"],movements:{god:["God keeps perfect accounts and will judge rightly. How does that free you?","Joseph said, \"Am I in the place of God?\" What did he understand about God?","How much has God forgiven you? Try to put it into words.","What does God ask of you toward the person who hurt you?"],heart:["What do you feel this person owes you?","What do you get out of holding on to this: a sense of power, protection, or being right?","How has this bitterness spread into other relationships or into how you see God?","Are you waiting for them to change before you will let go?"],gospel:["In the parable, the servant forgiven a huge debt choked another over a small one. Where do you see yourself?","Forgiveness is a promise not to bring the debt up against them. What would that look like here?","Forgiving isn't saying it didn't matter or that trust is instantly restored. How does that help you?","How could you do good to this person or pray for them this week?"]},keywords:["bitter","resent","can't forgive","unforgiv","grudge","betray"]},{id:"parenting",title:"Parenting",heartFocus:"Parents are called to shepherd their children's hearts toward God, not just to manage their behavior. Our own hearts get exposed in the process.",counselorNote:null,passages:["Deuteronomy 6:4\u20139","Ephesians 6:1\u20134","Proverbs 4:20\u201327","Colossians 3:20\u201321","Psalm 103:13\u201314"],openers:["Tell me about your kids. What do you enjoy about each one?","What's the hardest part of parenting right now?"],movements:{god:["God is a Father who has compassion on His children and remembers they are dust. How does He parent you?","God tells parents to talk about Him throughout ordinary days. What does that look like in your home?","God tells fathers not to provoke their children to anger. Why do you think He included that?","Your children belong first to the Lord. How does that change your role?"],heart:["When your child disobeys, what do you feel most: hurt for God's honor, or embarrassment, inconvenience, or frustration?","What do you need your children to be or do so that you feel like a good parent?","Where do you rely on rules and rewards instead of reaching your child's heart?","How have your own parents shaped what you expect?"],gospel:["God shows patience and grace to you when you fail. How could your children see that in you?","When did you last ask your child for forgiveness? What might that teach them?","What question could you ask your child to understand what they were wanting or believing?","How could you point your child to Jesus, not just to better behavior, next time?"]},keywords:["my son","my daughter","my kids","children","parent","teenager","my child"]},{id:"addiction",title:"Addiction",heartFocus:"Addiction is worship gone wrong: something good or harmful becomes the thing I run to for life. Christ is the one who satisfies and sets free.",counselorNote:"Watch for medical safety, such as withdrawal, and involve doctors when needed.",passages:["Romans 6:15\u201323","Galatians 5:1, 16\u201325","1 Corinthians 10:12\u201314","Isaiah 55:1\u20133","John 8:31\u201336"],openers:["How has this been affecting your life day to day?","What made you decide to talk about it now?"],movements:{god:["God invites the thirsty to come and drink for free. What are you really thirsty for?","God promises a way of escape in every temptation. Have you seen that in your life?","What does it mean that you are not your own, but bought with a price?","What does God call you to flee from, and what does He call you to run toward?"],heart:["What does this substance or habit give you: relief, numbness, confidence, escape?","When you reach for it, what do you believe about God in that moment?","Who or what have you sacrificed for it?","What lies does it whisper: \"just once,\" \"I deserve it,\" \"no one will know\"?"],gospel:["Jesus says if the Son sets you free, you will be free indeed. What would that freedom look like?","The Spirit produces self-control as fruit. How might you depend on Him rather than on willpower?","Who in the church could know the truth and walk with you daily?","What will you do in the hour when the craving is strongest?"]},keywords:["drink","drunk","alcohol","drugs","addict","high","relapse","gambl","pills"]},{id:"identity",title:"Identity",heartFocus:"We all look for something to tell us who we are and whether we matter. God defines us as His creatures and, in Christ, as His beloved children.",counselorNote:null,passages:["Genesis 1:26\u201328","Ephesians 1:3\u201314","Galatians 2:20","1 John 3:1\u20133","2 Corinthians 5:17"],openers:["How would you describe yourself to someone who just met you?","What do you think other people see when they look at you?"],movements:{god:["God made you in His image. What does that say about your worth?","God is the Creator, and we are His creatures. How does that settle who gets to define you?","What does it mean that the Father chose His people in Christ before the world began?","What does God call His children to become?"],heart:["What do you lean on most to feel like you're somebody: your looks, success, a relationship, being needed, how you feel?","What happens inside you when that is taken away or threatened?","Whose voice tells you who you are most loudly?","Where have you made your feelings or desires the final word on who you are?"],gospel:["John says the Father loves us so much that He calls us His children. What would change if you really believed that?","If you are in Christ, you are a new creation. What old labels are you still wearing?","How could your identity in Christ shape one choice you make this week?","Where could you serve others from security rather than trying to earn your worth?"]},keywords:["worthless","who i am","not enough","failure","identity","compare","approval"]},{id:"suffering",title:"Suffering",heartFocus:"Suffering makes us ask whether God is good and whether He's in control. Scripture says yes to both, and it shows a Savior who suffered with us and for us.",counselorNote:null,passages:["Romans 8:18\u201339","2 Corinthians 12:7\u201310","Job 38\u201342","1 Peter 4:12\u201319","Hebrews 4:14\u201316"],openers:["What have you been going through?","How are you holding up, really?"],movements:{god:["God works all things together for good for those who love Him. What does \"good\" mean there?","When Job met God, God didn't explain everything; He showed Himself. What does that tell you?","God's grace is enough, and His power is made perfect in weakness. Where have you felt weak?","What does God ask of you while you suffer?"],heart:["What have you been saying to God, or about God, in this?","What were you counting on that this suffering has taken?","Has this pushed you toward God or away from Him?","Are you tempted to believe God owes you an explanation, or that He doesn't care?"],gospel:["Jesus is a high priest who sympathizes with our weakness. How could you draw near to Him today?","Nothing can separate you from the love of God in Christ. Which of those \"nothings\" do you need to hear right now?","How might God be shaping you through this, not just getting you through it?","How could you entrust yourself to Him and keep doing good this week?"]},keywords:["suffer","pain","illness","cancer","diagnos","why god","hardship","chronic"]}])},948,[859]);
